_model: news-post
---
title: MAN Network: Back from the Field
---
pub_date: 2026-02-01
---
body:

We’re back from the outdoors. Last month the MAN team conducted a one-day field recording at Yema Haizi, a highland lake near Kangding in western Sichuan, China.

<div class="news-card-image">
  <figure>
    <img src="/files/man-field-2026-1.jpg" alt="A southwest-facing view (toward Moxi-Yagtya Ge 磨西-雅家梗) from the center of Yema Haizi, with North Ridge of Minya Konka (Mount Gongga) in the distance." loading="lazy">
    <figcaption>A southwest-facing view from the center of Yema Haizi, with North Ridge of Minya Konka (Mount Gongga) in the distance.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

Catch the full update on Mastodon: [@mantle_sound](https://mastodon.social/@mantle_sound/115982926151452979).

**Update (August 2026):** A new sound report is available for reviewing: [Running field-audio-tools on a long dual-mic F3 take](/software/running-field-audio-tools-on-a-long-f3-take/).
